course: dictionary
lesson: 7699
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it, which are its context. «Cooking is Dad's province.» Dad is not living in a country here, so province must mean the thing he is in charge of, his area of responsibility.
explain: Province can also mean a large part of a country that has its own local government, like Ontario in Canada. «His mom lives in BC, the province next door.» The words next door tell you the province is a region close by, inside the same country.
explain: Always check your meaning by swapping it in. «Cooking is Dad's area of responsibility» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. If it does not fit, look for a different meaning.
fact: A province is a large part of a country with its own local government.
fact: Canada has ten provinces and three territories.
fact: In the UK, «the provinces» means all of a country outside the capital city.
fact: Ireland has four old provinces: Leinster, Munster, Connacht and Ulster.
fact: Province can also mean an area of knowledge or responsibility, as in «Cooking is Dad's province.»
exercise: «Cooking is Dad's province.» What does province mean here? | A large part of a country with its own local government | A group of churches under an archbishop | A river bend on a map | *An area of responsibility, the thing Dad is in charge of
exercise: «His mom lives in BC, the province next door.» What is a province in this sentence? | *A large part of a country with its own local government | The capital city of a country | A kind of map scale | A type of weather
exercise: Which country has four old provinces: Leinster, Munster, Connacht and Ulster? | France | *Ireland | Wales
test: In the UK, what does «the provinces» mean? | A church with a bishop in charge | *All of a country outside the capital city | The very top of a mountain | A kind of school
test: «A valley and the mountain above it can have very different weather in the same province.» What is a province here? | A type of weather | A river bend on a map | *A large part of a country with its own local government | An area of knowledge
exam: Which sentence uses province to mean an area of knowledge or responsibility? | «Zoomed in on one province, you see every river bend.» | «In Calgary, Brayden lives with his dad.» | *«Cooking is Dad's province.» | «The province of Quebec is very large.»
